    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "You are an expert technical recruiter and career coach.\nAnalyze the provided Job Description against the candidate's resume and extract the required information based on the requested output schema.\n\nRULES:\n- Determine \"is_match\" using this rule: true if at least 70% of required skills match, false otherwise.\n- If visa requirements are not mentioned, output \"Not specified in the job description\".\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not include markdown formatting or code blocks.\n-Extract the link to apply for the job the directs to the application portal\n- Write a persuasive, 3-paragraph \"cover_letter\" explicitly connecting my resume projects (like ReserveBag or Apothecary Garden) to the responsibilities in the Job Description. Keep it under 250 words.\n\nRESUME SUMMARY:\nName: B Karthik | Location: Hyderabad, India | Fresh Graduate: May 2025\nSkills: C#, .NET 8, ASP.NET Core, React.js, JavaScript, Tailwind CSS, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, Supabase, Entity Framework Core, ADO.NET, Docker, Git, GitHub, Vercel, Render, REST APIs, OOP, MVC, AI/ML (YOLOv8, Computer Vision)\nProjects:\n- ReserveBag: Full-stack e-commerce app (React + .NET 8 + PostgreSQL + Supabase + Docker)\n- Apothecary Garden: AI plant app (React + Gemini Vision API + LocalStorage + Vercel)\n- Italian Wildlife AI Web App: Real-time object detection and tracking\n- Student Management System: Desktop app (C# + SQL Server + ADO.NET)\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION TO EVALUATE:\nCompany: {{ $json.company_name }}\nJob Title: {{ $json.title }}\nLocation: {{ $json.location }}.\nApply Link: {{ $json.source_link || $json.share_link }}\n\nJob Description:\n{{ $json.description }}\n\nEvaluate this JD against my resume. Return a JSON object with EXACTLY these keys: is_match, company_name, job_title, match_score, matching_skills, missing_skills, experience_relevance, location_compatibility, visa_requirements, recommendation, interview_prep,apply_link, cover_letter.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=={{ $json.description\n $json.sourse_link }}"
            }
          ]
        },
